("api/frame-title" :names ("frame-title" "(setf frame-title)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the frame title, including the title initially supplied to MAKE-FRAME. Returned strings survive later metadata queries and destruction." :position 149546)
("api/gauge" :names ("gauge") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Parent-owned progress indicator; supports inherited window operations. Positive range, value from zero through range, horizontal or vertical orientation. IDs, position, size, validator and native name use wxWidgets defaults; custom styles, taskbar progress and two-step creation remain unbound." :position 150958)
("api/gauge-range" :names ("gauge-range" "(setf gauge-range)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or assign the maximum progress. Assignment clamps the current native value to the new range and restores determinate mode by calling SetRange followed by SetValue. After a pulse the preserved value is platform-dependent; explicitly set GAUGE-VALUE when resuming measured work." :position 152765)
("api/gauge-value" :names ("gauge-value" "(setf gauge-value)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read determinate progress. After PULSE-GAUGE the reading is platform-dependent; do not interpret it as completed work. Assigning a value restores determinate mode without events." :position 154432)
("api/gauge-vertical-p" :names ("gauge-vertical-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query construction orientation; this property has no writer." :position 155851)
("api/handler-alive-p" :names ("handler-alive-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Observe native lifetime without dereferencing dead windows. Native weak tracking makes window destruction safe even with event processing disabled. A failed/uninitialized Lisp wrapper has no handle and signals NATIVE-ERROR. Session cleanup invalidates every identity; outside a session this query signals NATIVE-ERROR." :position 156760)
("api/handler-enabled-p" :names ("handler-enabled-p" "(setf handler-enabled-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read or write the native wxEvtHandler event-processing flag. Separate from window ENABLED-P/input state: disabled handlers can skip callbacks without greying the control. Native propagation rules still apply. Scoped contexts support Skip/propagation and checked close/notify veto; arbitrary pushed handlers remain unbound. In standalone chains this affects only the node itself, not processing by following nodes." :position 158742)
("api/handler-unlinked-p" :names ("handler-unlinked-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read native IsUnlinked without changing native ownership or queue membership. An unlinked wrapper remains strongly registered and its native object remains session-owned until explicit destruction or cleanup." :position 161080)
("api/idle-mode" :names ("idle-mode" "(setf idle-mode)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read/change process-wide wxIdleEvent GetMode/SetMode in the managed GUI session. Save/restore pre-session native policy at finish, including error cleanup. This is not a synthetic event field or effective per-window eligibility query." :position 162335)
