("api/on-click" :names ("on-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :CLICK snapshots with no payload. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 242535)
("api/on-selection" :names ("on-selection") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :SELECTION snapshots with selected index or NIL. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached. ABI38 LIST-BOX specialization manages its convenience :LISTBOX-SELECTION observer; generic bindings remain separately managed. Selection snapshots include cached native event text/index." :position 244373)
("api/on-text-change" :names ("on-text-change") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TEXT-CHANGE snapshots with copied text. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 246603)
("api/on-toggle" :names ("on-toggle") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace and release any prior handler. Receive :TOGGLE snapshots with boolean state. Callback conditions never unwind through C++; they are re-signaled at a Lisp boundary. Command callbacks are observers: the bridge calls Skip after delivery so remaining native bindings/parent routing can proceed. Generic subscriptions coexist with this one replacement slot. Optional contextual generic bindings can consume commands before later native handlers are reached." :position 248428)
("api/owned-event" :names ("owned-event") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed CLOS construction supports subclasses, slot initargs, defaults and AFTER hooks. Native origin is NIL. Mixed ancestry with EVENT-HANDLER/window is invalid. Explicit destruction or session cleanup owns deletion; there is no GC finalizer." :position 250221)
("api/panel" :names ("panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "CLOS wrapper for a child wxPanel." :position 252376)
("api/pending-events-p" :names ("pending-events-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Query wxAppConsole::HasPendingEvents across the current application. Does not report OS input, idle work or timers that have not queued an event. It is an observation, not a guarantee about the next dispatch. Safe to query during callbacks." :position 253441)
("api/pop-event-handler" :names ("pop-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Detach the top entry. Default preserves native owned registry/root; DELETE true releases bridge ownership before native PopEventHandler deletion and clears canonical roots/bindings. Empty stacks reject instead of invoking native assertions." :position 254549)
("api/post-event" :names ("post-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post an independent detached copy with wxPostEvent/AddPendingEvent; attach the receiver as copy origin. Input stays live/unchanged and may be destroyed or changed immediately. Delivery is asynchronous in the managed GUI session." :position 256135)
("api/previous-handler" :names ("previous-handler" "(setf previous-handler)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the native previous link. SETF mirrors NEXT-HANDLER, joining vacant source-previous/peer-next endpoints reciprocally or detaching one edge for NIL. Self/cycle/conflicting occupied endpoints reject before mutation; an existing reciprocal pair is idempotent." :position 257753)
("api/process-event" :names ("process-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously dispatch a fresh owned synthetic event through ProcessEvent, copy final veto state and then delete the event. Observer callbacks may run while handled-p is NIL because they Skip; native consumption/default handling determines the first result. Final veto is independent of handled-p and may be true from initial VETOED-P even without a matching handler. Close dispatch can run frame defaults. Callback errors re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary; handled nested errors do not stop RUN. No final values are returned when a condition escapes, and earlier callback mutations are not rolled back. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 259898)
("api/process-event-locally" :names ("process-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Synchronously process an independent detached copy with ProcessEventLocally, including local pre-processing and native chained handlers, without normal outer global-filter/parent/application fallback. Source remains live/unchanged. Observer delivery can return handled NIL; final veto is independent. Native local static/default handlers may still execute, including frame-close behavior; local processing is not observer-only or a no-default-action mode." :position 264331)
("api/process-events" :names ("process-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Yield to GUI events and process idle work without waiting for new input; re-signal callback errors after returning from native polling." :position 266529)
("api/process-pending-events" :names ("process-pending-events") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Dispatch queued wx events for all pending handlers of the bridge application via ProcessPendingEvents. Does not yield to OS input or run ProcessIdle. Does not wait for new events; callback duration and continuously requeued work may delay return. Callback conditions are contained at the native boundary and re-signaled afterwards." :position 267535)
("api/process-window-event" :names ("process-window-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Process a detached copy through native GetEventHandler stack routing, window and normal parent/application fallback. Source remains alive/unchanged; copy origin is WINDOW and callback source can be a pushed handler. Callback conditions re-signal at the nearer Lisp boundary." :position 269170)
("api/process-window-event-locally" :names ("process-window-event-locally") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Search the window and its pushed handlers with local pre-processing/validators, without normal upward window propagation. Process an independent detached copy with receiver-window origin and unchanged source. Observer delivery may still return handled NIL. Native local static/default handlers can still run, including frame-close behavior; local routing is not observer-only." :position 270744)
("api/pulse-gauge" :names ("pulse-gauge") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Request platform-native indeterminate progress. Call periodically while keeping the GUI event loop responsive. Visual animation and value readings vary by platform; no timer, worker dispatch or completion event is provided. SETF GAUGE-VALUE restores determinate mode." :position 272534)
("api/push-event-handler" :names ("push-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Push above the existing stack top while keeping native ownership in the bridge registry. Reject linked/attached or borrowed window/app peers, active session bindings and queued session events before mutation." :position 273821)
("api/queue-click" :names ("queue-click") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Post a button click for later dispatch. It uses the handler registered at dispatch time, including any replacement." :position 275313)
("api/queue-event" :names ("queue-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Queue a copied synthetic event: wxCommandEvent for seven command kinds, wxCloseEvent for close/session kinds and wxIdleEvent for :IDLE. Ordinary control properties are not changed directly. A queued close on a frame may run its native default closing action; use CLOSE-WINDOW for a synchronous acceptance result. Explicit UTF-8 lengths preserve text. Close events take no command payload, may be vetoable or non-vetoable, and do not normally propagate to parents. Registry types create wxCommandEvent or wxNotifyEvent according to their declared family. Initial veto applies only to custom notify types. Queuing offers no final veto/handled result; use PROCESS-EVENT when a synchronous decision is required. Owned-event dispatch always clones, attaches the receiver as copy origin and never consumes or mutates the source. The original can be destroyed after queueing or inside callbacks. Processing returns final state from its copy; contextual CLONE-EVENT can retain changed state detached from origin." :position 276288)
("api/radio-box" :names ("radio-box") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Explicitly owned mutually exclusive group; generic SELECTION/SETF, ITEM-COUNT and ITEM-TEXT methods." :position 281278)
("api/realize-toolbar" :names ("realize-toolbar") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "TOOLBAR with at least one tool or separator." :position 282522)
("api/register-event-type" :names ("register-event-type") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Allocate a process-local native event type and map NAME in the active session. Duplicate names, built-ins and unsupported families are rejected before registration. Names cannot be unregistered or replaced during this session. Registrations are session-wide metadata, not rolled back when an unrelated resource initializer fails. Native type IDs are not stable across processes." :position 283449)
("api/remove-event-handler" :names ("remove-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Preflight membership and detach without deletion. A live detached handler or handler belonging to another window returns NIL unchanged; only present entries reach native RemoveEventHandler, avoiding its absent-entry assertion." :position 285191)
("api/replace-text" :names ("replace-text") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Replace half-open native [FROM,TO) with VALUE using native Replace and text-change notification. Equal endpoints insert, empty VALUE removes. Mutation may precede a callback condition rethrow; handled conditions permit recovery. Exact no-op event counts, caret/selection and undo effects are port-specific." :position 286751)
("api/resume-event-propagation" :names ("resume-event-propagation") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Restore the native propagation level without changing Skip. Zero is allowed and keeps propagation stopped. Invalid LEVEL signals TYPE-ERROR; expired contexts reject native access." :position 288204)
("api/return-to-application-repl" :names ("return-to-application-repl") :kind :restart :kind-name "Restart" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Abandon the failing REPL evaluation or callback operation using the active debugger restart." :position 289968)
("api/run" :names ("run") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Block until STOP or the last top-level frame closes. Callback errors are re-signaled after returning from native code." :position 290779)
("api/scroll-extent" :names ("scroll-extent") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. Read-only." :position 291690)
("api/scroll-position" :names ("scroll-position" "(setf scroll-position)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF exact pair0..1000000 scroll units." :position 292573)
("api/scroll-rate" :names ("scroll-rate" "(setf scroll-rate)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "SCROLLED-PANEL. SETF value is exact two-integer list0..256 pixels/unit." :position 293892)
("api/scrolled-panel" :names ("scrolled-panel") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary ":parent required, :scroll-rate exact pair0..256 default(0 16), subclass initargs." :position 295200)
("api/selection" :names ("selection" "(setf selection)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read current selection: an index for CHOICE/LIST-BOX/NOTEBOOK, or a canonical managed TREE-ITEM view for TREE-CONTROL, with NIL when no selection exists. Reader NOTIFY is ignored. Writes are silent by default; notifying choice/list writes emit synthetic events, while notebook/tree writes use native vetoable selection. Return of a requested assignment does not prove native acceptance. Populated tree writes require a live same-tree item; NIL is empty-tree no-op only. Root creation and structural edits silently normalize valid selection before idle. RADIO-BOX always has exactly one valid index; its explicit notifying write commits before a native-class command event, without veto or rollback. COMBO-BOX selection writes also set item text; NIL clears both text and selection. Arbitrary text writes do not promise a selected item." :position 296458)
("api/show-modal" :names ("show-modal") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Run the native modal loop. Supported from menu/event callbacks, RUN or a pump; nested public SHOW-MODAL calls reject. Outer event contexts suspend during the modal call and become usable again after it returns; callbacks entered by the modal loop have their own valid innermost contexts. Bare callback errors cancel the modal operation and re-signal the primary condition after unwind. A nested notifying operation whose condition is handled locally can recover without cancelling. Manual RUN/pump/finish and structural menu edits remain guarded. Native close of the current dialog is consumed and cancels it; ancestor close events are consumed while modal. Public CLOSE-WINDOW on a protected ancestor rejects. Generic file UI prompts are redirected to guarded generic message dialogs. Internal prompts suspend borrowed contexts; errors or public cancellation unwind internal-to-outer sequentially. Cancelling an inner prompt normally returns to the outer dialog. Nested public SHOW-MODAL remains forbidden." :position 301082)
("api/show-window" :names ("show-window") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Show with true SHOW, hide with NIL. Existing one-argument calls still show the window and return it as their primary value." :position 304456)
("api/shown-p" :names ("shown-p" "(setf shown-p)") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Read the window's own shown flag. A hidden ancestor does not change this flag; it does not report effective screen visibility." :position 305730)
("api/single-choice-dialog" :names ("single-choice-dialog") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Construct a modal-only native single-choice dialog. Selection is always an in-range nonnegative index; NIL is not a choice. Strings are Unicode without NUL; empty strings are accepted. Defaults/subclass slot initargs and AFTER hooks use the native-backed CLOS protocol. Failed managed initialization destroys newly created resources; it does not reverse arbitrary external mutations." :position 307113)
("api/slider" :names ("slider") :kind :class :kind-name "Class" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Native-backed slider, :parent required, :minimum0/:maximum100/:value0, :orientation :horizontal or :vertical." :position 309787)
