("api/ui-timer-active-p" :names ("ui-timer-active-p") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Owner/ancestor expiry removes registration/root. Periodic activity persists through a function until cancel/expiry; escaping errors cancel the offending timer." :position 361346)
("api/ui-timer-p" :names ("ui-timer-p") :kind :function :kind-name "Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Pure Lisp structure predicate; works outside an application session." :position 362689)
("api/unbind-event" :names ("unbind-event") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Remove exactly one registration, including from inside itself or another callback. The current callback may finish; later deliveries cannot invoke the removed function. Releases generic callback roots. A live native binding object is retained until an active callback returns. Unbinding destroys the native user-data adapter and releases global association roots, but active dispatch frames and saved snapshots can keep the Lisp value alive." :position 363263)
("api/unlink-event-handler" :names ("unlink-event-handler") :kind :generic-function :kind-name "Generic Function" :package "WXLAMBDA" :summary "Splice the native previous/next neighbors together, then detach both source edges. Does not destroy the handler, transfer ownership or move its pending queue. Already unlinked input is harmless. This differs from SETF NIL, which detaches one edge only." :position 365240)
